What a deployment runs, and what it deliberately does not
One OSGi container holds the shipped distribution: every bundle that touches
tenant data, a face per FHIR version and a runtime per tenant, over
PostgreSQL with a database per tenant. Beside it run plain jars, each its own
process with its own credentials: the operator that provisions against
Kubernetes, the fleet reader that reads a deployment from outside, and the
verifier that checks a sealed archive with no network. A development console
is drawn apart and dashed because it binds tenant-plane services and is kept
out of the serving distribution for that reason.
